   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Modals of supposition",
     "texto": [
      "Modals can express the speaker's assessment: **Er muss krank sein** (he must be ill; a strong deduction), **Er dürfte zu Hause sein** (he is probably at home), **Er kann müde sein** (he may be tired). They are not mathematical degrees of certainty: context and intonation matter. **Er muss arbeiten** usually expresses obligation, but the context can also allow a deduction reading."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Supposition about the past",
     "texto": [
      "To assess an earlier situation, use the modal + **Partizip II + haben/sein**: **Er muss gestern krank gewesen sein** (he must have been ill yesterday); **Sie kann die Nachricht nicht erhalten haben** (she may not have received the news). In these constructions the auxiliary appears at the end in the infinitive."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "sollen and wollen of another person",
     "texto": [
      "**Er soll reich sein** (they say he is rich, according to others). **Er will Arzt sein** (he says he is a doctor, according to himself). Here the modal shows that the information comes from another person, not from us."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
